  #line-at(191.624pt, 86.303pt, "max")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.09pt, 83.78pt, " of MLFE droplets in agreement with experiments. Our findings ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 106.82pt, "provide valuable insights into the novel realm of field dictated LFE, and hold significant ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 127.46pt, "implications towards the design of frictionless, rapid colloid droplet transport systems, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 148.22pt, "targeted droplet manipulation/activation for advanced thermal management. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 197.54pt, "Keywords")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.02pt, 197.54pt, ":")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.98pt, 197.54pt, " Magneto-Leidenfrost effect; droplets; dynamic Leidenfrost effect, ferrofluids; ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 218.3pt, "magnetic field; ferrohydrodynamics  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.61pt, "1. Introduction")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.02pt, 307.85pt, "Impact or interactions of a droplet on a heated surface, at temperatures significantly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 328.49pt, "above the boiling point of the liquid, culminates in rapid evaporation generated vapour layer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 349.25pt, "between the droplet and the substrate. This intervening vapour layer, often micron-level thick, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 369.89pt, "prevents direct solid-liquid contact, and acts as a near-frictionless cushion that enables the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 390.65pt, "droplet to levitate, hover, or propel above the surface. The vapour layer behaves as an ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 411.29pt, "insulating film, diminishing the heat transfer, and thereby resulting in a significant increase in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 432.07pt, "phase transition time. First observed by a physician, J. G. Leidenfrost [1] in 1756, it is known ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 452.71pt, "as the Leidenfrost effect (LFE). The LFE exhibits a dualistic paradigm. On one hand, it is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 473.47pt, "highly undesired regime to heat transfer-based design considerations in a myriad of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 494.11pt, "applications, such as spray cooling in fire extinguishment, and electronics cooling systems ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 514.87pt, "[2,3], material quenching [4], cooling of nuclear fuel rods [5], and fuel drop impingement in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 535.51pt, "internal-combustion engines [6]. On the contrary, it provides opportunities for controlling ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 556.27pt, "preferential motion and self-propulsion of droplets [7-9] in advanced thermofluidic devices. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 577.51pt, "For gently deposited droplets, the Leidenfrost temperature (LFT, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.09pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(414.124pt, 580.026pt, "L")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.257pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(407.712pt, 577.608pt, "T")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.46pt, 577.51pt, ") corresponds to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.58pt, "maximum droplet evaporation time. However, for impinging droplets, the corresponding ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 621.82pt, "dynamic Leidenfrost temperature (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.053pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(254.195pt, 624.261pt, "DL")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.211pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(247.336pt, 621.849pt, "T")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(265.73pt, 621.82pt, ") is identified as the lowest surface temperature at ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 644.86pt, "which onset of droplet rebound occurs with minimal spraying or droplet disintegration [10-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 665.5pt, "13]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 694.3pt, "Existing theoretical works include investigations on shape [14] and geometry [15] of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 714.94pt, "Leidenfrost droplets, and the underlying vapour layer, and models predicting Leidenfrost ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 735.7pt, "temperature [14,16-19]. The Leidenfrost temperature is determined by balancing dynamic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 756.336pt, "pressure due to droplet impact with the vapour pressure supporting the droplet levitation. ")
]

