  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(237.53pt, 540.91pt, ". They attribute this behaviour to the enhanced heat transfer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 563.95pt, "through the larger contact spread-area at higher impact velocities [28,30,37]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 592.63pt, "In the recent past, surface modification-based approaches have been explored towards  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 613.42pt, "control over LFT. Micro-textured surfaces, which behave as micropillars and penetrate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 634.06pt, "through the vapour layer, thereby suppressing droplet levitation by rewetting the surface ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 654.82pt, "[17,38,39] have been studied. For higher pillar density, however, the increased capillary ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 675.46pt, "wetting ceases to dominate and de-wetting vapour pressure increases due to enlarged heat ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 696.22pt, "transfer area and enhanced flow resistance to escaping vapour, resulting in decrease in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 716.86pt, "Leidenfrost temperature [40,41]. The highly mobile nature of Leidenfrost droplets has ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 737.62pt, "motivated extensive efforts towards their controlled and directional transport [7-9,42,43]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 758.256pt, "Linke et al. [7] and Lagubeau et al. [8] demonstrated that Leidenfrost droplets and levitating ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 7pt), 388.5pt, 334.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.89pt, 790.2pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.18pt, "dry-ice blocks, respectively, can self-propel on asymmetric ratchet surfaces due to vapour-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.82pt, "driven forces arising from the directional rectification of anisotropic vapour flow. Li et al. [9] ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.58pt, "used collective interactions between planar ratchet arrays to achieve enhanced ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 145.22pt, "manoeuvrability and control over Leidenfrost droplet transport. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 174.02pt, "Further, non-tactile stimulus-based methods [44-48] have proven effective for droplet ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 194.66pt, "actuation and control. Few works [49-51] have employed electric fields between Leidenfrost ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.42pt, "droplets and the substrate to suppress the droplet levitation and enhance heat transfer by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 236.06pt, "attracting droplets towards substrate using electrostatic forces. A handful studies [52,53] have ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.85pt, "explored the use of magnetic fields to trap Leidenfrost droplets and modulate their ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.49pt, "evaporation rates. While these studies partially address the practical limitations of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.25pt, "micro/nano-textured and ratcheted surfaces, such as complex and costly fabrication, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 318.89pt, "susceptibility to fouling, and limited scalability, they focus primarily on Levitation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 340.01pt, "suppression and are largely restricted to near-static droplets (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.126pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(398.106pt, 340.085pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.004pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.681pt, 342.503pt, "o")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.126pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(365.224pt, 340.085pt, "We")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.91pt, 340.01pt, "). ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 371.21pt, "In our novel approach, we employ magnetic field to alter the  very behaviour of impinging ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 391.85pt, "ferrofluid Leidenfrost droplets, a study that remains completely unexplored in the literature. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 412.61pt, "Unlike previous studies that manipulate Leidenfrost droplets through surface micro-texturing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 433.27pt, "[7,40], the present method is based on a contact-free external stimulus and does not require ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 454.03pt, "permanent modification of the substrate surface. Our research reveals that a carefully tailored ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 474.67pt, "combination of vertical and horizontal magnetic forces, applied via a non-uniform magnetic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 495.43pt, "field environment, can trigger  Leidenfrost rebound under conditions where droplets would ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 516.07pt, "otherwise remain grounded. We investigate thoroughly the associated ferro-hydrodynamics, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 536.83pt, "and their influence on magnetic-Leidenfrost effect (MLFE)-driven rebound conditions. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 557.47pt, "Supported by a theoretical model, we systematically examine the role of magnetic forces ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 578.23pt, "during different stages of droplet impact and spreading, and show how magnetic fields can be ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 598.87pt, "used to control impact outcomes for MLFE, over a wide range of impact conditions, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 619.66pt, "nanoparticle concentrations, and substrate superheats indicating the broad applicability of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 640.3pt, "method. We further demonstrate control over MLFE droplet residence time and the size of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 661.06pt, "daughter droplets produced during fragmentation by appropriately tuning the magnetic field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 681.7pt, "strength and substrate temperature. The findings reveal a new phenomenon of the MLFE in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 702.46pt, "ferrofluids, offer a potential route for frictionless and rapid droplet transport, targeted heat-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 723.1pt, "transfer modulation in thermal management applications, controlled reagent transport and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 743.856pt, "deposition, microdroplets sorting, and inkjet printing technologies. ")
]

