  #line-at(72.024pt, 148.22pt, "model assuming the outward vapour flow in the thin vapour layer as Poiseuille flow [14,50], ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 168.86pt, "and is found to be proportional to the square of droplet contact diameter. Also, an increase in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 189.62pt, "contact diameter means area available for heat transfer is more and availability of more ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 210.26pt, "nucleation sites, resulting in more production of vapour, favouring the LFE. In our study, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 231.02pt, "consideration of dynamic impact effects becomes essential. On one hand, the higher inertia of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 251.66pt, "impinging droplets results in larger spread diameter, which eventually favours the LFE by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 272.33pt, "increasing the vapour pressure [12,13,34-37]. On the contrary, however, for droplets with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 293.09pt, "high impact inertia to achieve LFE, the vapour pressure must be large enough to balance the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 313.73pt, "dynamic pressure arising due to impact momentum, and may require higher substrate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 334.49pt, "temperatures [23,32,33] to avoid splashing/fragmentation immediately post-impact. An ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 355.13pt, "experimental study by Mitchell et al. [55] revealed that the impact force is significant only for ")
